---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Process — Eight34 Labs" description="Three phases, small steps, nothing big-bang: Discover, Set Up, Tune & Grow — with what you get, what we need from you, and what happens after launch.">
  <main>
    <section class="page-hero">
      <p class="hero-label">Process</p>
      <h1>How we collaborate</h1>
      <p>Three phases. Small steps. Nothing big-bang.</p>
      <p>The same discipline from our engineering roots, applied to AI setup: understand first, build the smallest useful thing, then improve it with real use.</p>
      <div class="phase-strip">
        <span><strong>01</strong>Discover</span>
        <span><strong>02</strong>Set Up</span>
        <span><strong>03</strong>Tune &amp; Grow</span>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Three phases -->
    <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;">
      <div class="timeline">
        <div class="timeline-step">
          <span class="phase-chip">01</span>
          <h3>Discover</h3>
          <p>We meet at your business, watch how the week actually runs, and interview the people doing the work. You get a ranked, costed plan — including what we&rsquo;d leave alone.</p>
          <p style="margin-top: 12px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; color: var(--ink-400);">Starts with a conversation</p>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-step">
          <span class="phase-chip">02</span>
          <h3>Set Up</h3>
          <p>We configure the first workflow end-to-end: tools chosen, connected, tested with your real scenarios, and your team trained on it. One thing working beats five things half-working.</p>
          <p style="margin-top: 12px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; color: var(--ink-400);">Small, tested, trained</p>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-step">
          <span class="phase-chip">03</span>
          <h3>Tune &amp; Grow</h3>
          <p>We review what&rsquo;s saving time and what isn&rsquo;t, fix the friction, and only then add the next improvement. You always know what each piece costs and what it returns.</p>
          <p style="margin-top: 12px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; color: var(--ink-400);">Ongoing, at your pace</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top: 28px;">
        <a class="btn-primary" href="/contact" style="padding: 10px 22px; font-size: 14px;">Contact Us →</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Standards -->
    <section class="section" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--ink-150);">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Our standards</h2>
        <p>How we work, in writing</p>
      </div>
      <div class="standards-grid">
        <div class="standard-card">
          <h3>Honest scoping</h3>
          <p>If AI won&rsquo;t help a task, we say so — and leave it out of the quote.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="standard-card">
          <h3>Your accounts, your data</h3>
          <p>Everything is set up under your ownership. No lock-in, no hostage logins.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="standard-card">
          <h3>Tested before launch</h3>
          <p>Every automation is tried against your real questions and edge cases first.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="standard-card">
          <h3>Plain-English handover</h3>
          <p>Guides your newest hire can follow, plus training for the team.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="standard-card">
          <h3>Costs up front</h3>
          <p>Tool subscriptions and our fees, itemized separately, before work begins.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>



    <!-- Closing CTA -->
    <section class="section" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--ink-150); padding-bottom: 90px;">
      <div class="contact-cta-box">
        <h2>Phase 01 starts with a conversation</h2>
        <p>Tell us how your week runs, and we will map the first step.</p>
        <div class="contact-cta-actions">
          <a class="btn-primary" href="/contact" style="padding: 12px 24px; font-size: 14.5px;">Contact Us →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
